---
source: tests/help.rs
expression: help
---
Manage a Control D account over its REST API.

cdctl is not ctrld: ctrld is Control D's DNS daemon and runs DNS on a machine; cdctl manages the
account behind it. They coexist.

Usage: cdctl [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  api          Raw request against the API origin (escape hatch; GET by default)
  auth         Authenticate cdctl with an API token
  profile      Inspect the account's profiles
  folder       Manage a profile's rule folders (API: groups)
  rule         Manage a profile's DNS rules
  config       Read and write cdctl's own configuration
  completions  Shell completion script (works without a token)
  reference    The full command surface as one Markdown document (works without a token)
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -p, --profile <PK|name>
          Profile to operate on (name or PK)
          
          [env: CONTROLD_PROFILE=]

      --json
          Emit JSON (full document) instead of a table

      --fields <a,b>
          Comma-separated JSON fields to keep; implies --json

      --plain
          Tables without borders, for awk/cut

  -y, --yes
          Skip confirmation prompts (ignored when the target profile is implicit)

      --no-retry
          Disable automatic retries (GETs only ever retry)

      --timeout <SECS>
          Per-request timeout in seconds

      --debug
          Request/response trace on stderr; token always redacted

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
